  Welcome to the World of Citadel BBSs.  There are many things you need to
 know over time, but here are the basics:  The BBS is a chain of rooms.  It
 is set up so that you can type simple commands with a great varity.
 These commands are:
  G(oto)      - Will "goto" a room with New unread messages.
  N(ew)       - Will read the new messages in the present room
  P(ause)     - Pauses the Message Display
  S(top)      - Stops the Message Display
  U(ngoto)    - Backs up to the last room
  T(erminate) - Logs off
  D(oor)      - Will bring up a list of Availible doors
  E(nter)     - Allows you to enter a message in a room

  .RE         - Make sure the period is in there.  It displays the files
                in the current room, if the room is a directory room.
  .RZB        - Will download a file with Zmodem, Substitute a Y for Ymodem,
                X for Xmodem, K for Kermit.
  .EZF        - Same as above, but upload a file instead of downloading.

  Those are the basic commands, and everything you need to get started.  To
 leave the sysop mail, type in the following carefully:  ".G Mail" to move to
 the mail room.  "E" to enter a message, and then either "Tony Preston" or
 "Sysop" to enter a message to sysop.  Enter the message, and then hit
 the RETURN key two times to bring a message command prompt up.  "S" will
 save the message.